{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"freemium pricing freemium pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","fileName":"Freemium Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Freemium Pricing","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:39\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cloud Pricing Models]] · [[Game Revenue and Markets]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","Software as a Service","Pay-to-Win","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"freemium pricing freemium pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","fileName":"Freemium Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Freemium Pricing","heading":"Freemium Pricing","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Freemium pricing provides a usable service without charge and earns revenue through a more capable paid version or through advertising associated with the free service. The free level is intended to attract and retain a broad user base.\n\nThe model fits [[Software as a Service]] because functionality can be limited or expanded centrally without distributing another application. The paid tier must offer enough added value to convert some free users while the free tier remains useful enough to sustain adoption.\n\nIn games, freemium pricing commonly sells premium items or downloadable content inside a free base experience. The free game must remain enjoyable rather than becoming crippleware, and selling competitive power can turn the model into [[Pay-to-Win]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","Software as a Service","Pay-to-Win","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"freemium pricing freemium pricing","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Freemium Pricing.md","fileName":"Freemium Pricing.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Freemium Pricing","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[cloudcomputing_mit.epub]]\n\n[[fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cloud Pricing Models","Game Revenue and Markets","Software as a Service","Pay-to-Win","cloudcomputing_mit.epub","fundamentalsofgamedesign3e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}